Item 01 is done. Nothing left depends on another result, and the loop is not complete, so no `LOOP_COMPLETE` line.

**What I built.** `learning/canonical.py` computes three canonical forms per instance (matrix digest, nauty certificate of the coloured customer–product bipartite graph, nauty certificate of the MOSP graph), the networkx WL hash, and the automorphism group order, with pynauty behind a soft import. It runs in under a second on 16 cores and writes `learning/data/canonical.csv` plus the tables. Seven tests on hand-checkable three-customer instances are in `tests/test_canonical.py`. The full suite passes (703 passed, 2 skipped, 1 xfailed, 66 s). Nothing under `solutions/` changed and no solver default was touched.

**What the corpus turns out to be.**

| level | classes |
|---|---:|
| instances | 6,376 |
| identical matrix | 6,332 |
| isomorphic matrix | 6,313 |
| isomorphic MOSP graph | 3,667 |

- **42.5% of the corpus is isomorphic copies.** The redundancy is a small-instance effect (44.6% at n ≤ 30, 13.2% at n > 30) and confined to Harvey and Simonis. Chu & Stuckey, SCOOP, Shaw and Wilson contain no duplicates at any level.
- **A quarter of the corpus is complete graphs.** 1,669 instances have optimum equal to n_customers with a complete MOSP graph. The four largest classes are K10, K15, K30 and K20.
- **The Challenge folder is a copy.** All 46 instances in `MOSP_Instances/Challenge` are the Miller, Shaw and Wilson originals, 44 byte-identical and 2 differing by one all-zero product column. Each is certified twice under two names.
- **File grouping leaks.** 157 graph classes span more than one source file, the largest spanning eleven. A split grouped by file still trains on copies of its test instances. The report recommends grouping by the new graph certificate before any grouped number from the earlier learning report is quoted again.
- **WL is safe here.** The WL hash merges only 14 of 3,667 classes, all sparse Harvey instances with optimum 3.
- **The audit passed.** Zero optimum disagreements within any isomorphism class, so no re-certification was needed.

Written up as section 1 of the new `reports/ml_nature.md`, with the regenerate command. `PROGRESS.md` has the iteration entry and the current count is 1/8, and item 01 is marked done in `iterations.md`. Next is item 02, which should use the graph certificate as its grouping key.

